<kml xmlns="http://www.opengis.net/kml/2.2"><Document><name>Divya Desam Yatra: 106 earthly Divya Desams</name><description>From the Divya Desam Yatra app. Coordinates from Wikipedia. Not-for-profit.</description>
<Style id="sCholaNadu"><IconStyle><color>ff1c1c8a</color><scale>1.1</scale><Icon><href>http://maps.google.com/mapfiles/kml/paddle/wht-blank.png</href></Icon></IconStyle></Style>
<Style id="sNaduNadu"><IconStyle><color>ff12a0c0</color><scale>1.1</scale><Icon><href>http://maps.google.com/mapfiles/kml/paddle/wht-blank.png</href></Icon></IconStyle></Style>
<Style id="sThondaiNadu"><IconStyle><color>ff736e0f</color><scale>1.1</scale><Icon><href>http://maps.google.com/mapfiles/kml/paddle/wht-blank.png</href></Icon></IconStyle></Style>
<Style id="sMalaiNadu"><IconStyle><color>ff2f8f3a</color><scale>1.1</scale><Icon><href>http://maps.google.com/mapfiles/kml/paddle/wht-blank.png</href></Icon></IconStyle></Style>
<Style id="sPandyaNadu"><IconStyle><color>ff8a1c6d</color><scale>1.1</scale><Icon><href>http://maps.google.com/mapfiles/kml/paddle/wht-blank.png</href></Icon></IconStyle></Style>
<Style id="sVadaNadu"><IconStyle><color>ff1a5fd0</color><scale>1.1</scale><Icon><href>http://maps.google.com/mapfiles/kml/paddle/wht-blank.png</href></Icon></IconStyle></Style>
<Folder><name>Chola Nadu</name><Placemark><name>1. Thiruvarangam</name><styleUrl>#sCholaNadu</styleUrl><description>Srirangam. Perumal: Ranganatha (Periya Perumal); utsavar Namperumal. Thayar: Ranganayaki. Posture: Reclining. The first Divya Desam, called simply Koil, &quot;the Temple&quot;. Eleven Azhwars sang here, and Sri Caitanya Mahaprabhu stayed four months of Caturmasya.</description><ExtendedData><Data name="Number"><value>1</value></Data><Data name="Region"><value>Chola Nadu</value></Data><Data name="Tamil"><value>திருவரங்கம்</value></Data></ExtendedData><Point><coordinates>78.6897,10.8625,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>2. Thirukkozhi</name><styleUrl>#sCholaNadu</styleUrl><description>Uraiyur (Nachiyar Koil, Woraiyur). Perumal: Azhagiya Manavalan. Thayar: Kamalavalli Nachiyar. Posture: Standing. Birthplace of Thiruppaan Azhwar. The Thayar has precedence here, and Namperumal of Srirangam comes as the bridegroom each Panguni.</description><ExtendedData><Data name="Number"><value>2</value></Data><Data name="Region"><value>Chola Nadu</value></Data><Data name="Tamil"><value>திருக்கோழி</value></Data></ExtendedData><Point><coordinates>78.67,10.82,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>3. Thirukkarambanur</name><styleUrl>#sCholaNadu</styleUrl><description>Uthamar Koil. Perumal: Purushottaman. Thayar: Poornavalli (Purushottama Nayaki). Posture: Reclining. One compound holds shrines of Vishnu, Shiva and Brahma with their consorts, so it is also called the Trimurti kshetram.</description><ExtendedData><Data name="Number"><value>3</value></Data><Data name="Region"><value>Chola Nadu</value></Data><Data name="Tamil"><value>திருக்கரம்பனூர்</value></Data></ExtendedData><Point><coordinates>78.81,10.49,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>4. Thiruvellarai</name><styleUrl>#sCholaNadu</styleUrl><description>Thiruvellarai. Perumal: Pundarikakshan. Thayar: Pankajavalli (Shenbagavalli). Posture: Standing. Tradition holds it older than Srirangam. Two gateways are used by season, one for Uttarayana and one for Dakshinayana.</description><ExtendedData><Data name="Number"><value>4</value></Data><Data name="Region"><value>Chola Nadu</value></Data><Data name="Tamil"><value>திருவெள்ளறை</value></Data></ExtendedData><Point><coordinates>78.67,10.96,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>5. Thiru Anbil</name><styleUrl>#sCholaNadu</styleUrl><description>Anbil. Perumal: Vadivazhagiya Nambi (Sundararajan). Thayar: Azhagiyavalli. Posture: Reclining. A quiet village shrine across the Kollidam from Koviladi, sung in a single verse by Thirumazhisai Azhwar.</description><ExtendedData><Data name="Number"><value>5</value></Data><Data name="Region"><value>Chola Nadu</value></Data><Data name="Tamil"><value>திருஅன்பில்</value></Data></ExtendedData><Point><coordinates>78.8822,10.8677,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>6. Thirupper Nagar</name><styleUrl>#sCholaNadu</styleUrl><description>Koviladi (Appakkudathan). Perumal: Appakkudathan (Appala Ranganathan). Thayar: Indravalli (Kamalavalli). Posture: Reclining. The Lord rests with a pot of appam by His hand. Nammazhwar&apos;s last decad on an earthly temple (Thiruvaimozhi 10.8) was sung here.</description><ExtendedData><Data name="Number"><value>6</value></Data><Data name="Region"><value>Chola Nadu</value></Data><Data name="Tamil"><value>திருப்பேர்நகர்</value></Data></ExtendedData><Point><coordinates>78.8891,10.8393,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>7. Thirukkandiyur</name><styleUrl>#sCholaNadu</styleUrl><description>Kandiyur. Perumal: Hara Sapa Vimochana Perumal. Thayar: Kamalavalli. Posture: Standing. Here the Lord freed Shiva from the curse of Brahma&apos;s skull that had stuck to his hand, hence the name.</description><ExtendedData><Data name="Number"><value>7</value></Data><Data name="Region"><value>Chola Nadu</value></Data><Data name="Tamil"><value>திருக்கண்டியூர்</value></Data></ExtendedData><Point><coordinates>79.1089,10.8603,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>8. Thirukkoodalur</name><styleUrl>#sCholaNadu</styleUrl><description>Aduthurai Perumal Koil. Perumal: Jagathrakshakan (Vaiyam Katha Perumal). Thayar: Padmasani (Pushpavalli). Posture: Standing. The devas gathered (koodal) here to pray when the earth was carried away, and the Lord protected the world.</description><ExtendedData><Data name="Number"><value>8</value></Data><Data name="Region"><value>Chola Nadu</value></Data><Data name="Tamil"><value>திருக்கூடலூர்</value></Data></ExtendedData><Point><coordinates>79.2035,10.9252,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>9. Thirukkavithalam</name><styleUrl>#sCholaNadu</styleUrl><description>Kapisthalam. Perumal: Gajendra Varadan. Thayar: Ramamanivalli (Potramaraiyal). Posture: Reclining. The place of Gajendra moksha in local tradition, and one of the five Krishnaranya kshetrams.</description><ExtendedData><Data name="Number"><value>9</value></Data><Data name="Region"><value>Chola Nadu</value></Data><Data name="Tamil"><value>திருக்கவித்தலம்</value></Data></ExtendedData><Point><coordinates>79.2565,10.9469,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>10. Thiruppullam Bhoothangudi</name><styleUrl>#sCholaNadu</styleUrl><description>Pullabhoothangudi. Perumal: Valvil Raman. Thayar: Hemambujavalli (Potramaraiyal). Posture: Reclining. Sri Rama rests here after performing the last rites for Jatayu, a rare reclining Rama.</description><ExtendedData><Data name="Number"><value>10</value></Data><Data name="Region"><value>Chola Nadu</value></Data><Data name="Tamil"><value>திருப்புள்ளம்பூதங்குடி</value></Data></ExtendedData><Point><coordinates>79.3034,10.9716,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>11. Thiru Adanur</name><styleUrl>#sCholaNadu</styleUrl><description>Adanur. Perumal: Andalakkum Aiyan. Thayar: Ranganayaki (Bhargavi). Posture: Reclining. The Lord lies with a grain measure as His pillow and a stylus and palm leaf in hand, the keeper of every account.</description><ExtendedData><Data name="Number"><value>11</value></Data><Data name="Region"><value>Chola Nadu</value></Data><Data name="Tamil"><value>திருஆதனூர்</value></Data></ExtendedData><Point><coordinates>79.3135,10.9765,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>12. Thirukkudanthai</name><styleUrl>#sCholaNadu</styleUrl><description>Kumbakonam (Sarangapani). Perumal: Aravamudhan (Sarangapani). Thayar: Komalavalli. Posture: Reclining. Nathamuni heard the &quot;Aravamude&quot; decad sung here and went in search of the lost four thousand verses. The whole Divya Prabandham was recovered because of this temple.</description><ExtendedData><Data name="Number"><value>12</value></Data><Data name="Region"><value>Chola Nadu</value></Data><Data name="Tamil"><value>திருக்குடந்தை</value></Data></ExtendedData><Point><coordinates>79.375,10.9596,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>13. Thiruvinnagar</name><styleUrl>#sCholaNadu</styleUrl><description>Oppiliappan Koil. Perumal: Oppiliappan (Thiruvinnagarappan). Thayar: Bhumi Devi. Posture: Standing. All offerings are cooked without salt, in memory of the Lord&apos;s promise to the young Bhumi Devi&apos;s father, Markandeya.</description><ExtendedData><Data name="Number"><value>13</value></Data><Data name="Region"><value>Chola Nadu</value></Data><Data name="Tamil"><value>திருவிண்ணகர்</value></Data></ExtendedData><Point><coordinates>79.4321,10.9616,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>14. Thirunaraiyur</name><styleUrl>#sCholaNadu</styleUrl><description>Nachiyar Koil. Perumal: Srinivasan (Thirunaraiyur Nambi). Thayar: Vanjulavalli (Nambikkai Nachiyar). Posture: Standing. The Lord Himself gave pancha-samskara to Thirumangai Azhwar here. Thayar leads every procession, and the stone Kal Garuda grows heavier at each gate.</description><ExtendedData><Data name="Number"><value>14</value></Data><Data name="Region"><value>Chola Nadu</value></Data><Data name="Tamil"><value>திருநறையூர்</value></Data></ExtendedData><Point><coordinates>79.4456,10.9158,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>15. Thirucherai</name><styleUrl>#sCholaNadu</styleUrl><description>Thirucherai. Perumal: Saranathan. Thayar: Saranayaki (Sara Nachiyar). Posture: Standing. Pancha Sara kshetram: the Lord, Thayar, vimanam, tank and town all bear the name Sara. River Kaveri did penance here.</description><ExtendedData><Data name="Number"><value>15</value></Data><Data name="Region"><value>Chola Nadu</value></Data><Data name="Tamil"><value>திருச்சேறை</value></Data></ExtendedData><Point><coordinates>79.4544,10.8791,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>16. Thirukkannamangai</name><styleUrl>#sCholaNadu</styleUrl><description>Thirukannamangai. Perumal: Bhaktavatsala Perumal (Patharavi Perumal). Thayar: Abhishekavalli. Posture: Standing. The devas are said to remain as bees in the hive at the Thayar shrine, to keep seeing the divine wedding.</description><ExtendedData><Data name="Number"><value>16</value></Data><Data name="Region"><value>Chola Nadu</value></Data><Data name="Tamil"><value>திருக்கண்ணமங்கை</value></Data></ExtendedData><Point><coordinates>79.5866,10.7996,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>17. Thirukkannapuram</name><styleUrl>#sCholaNadu</styleUrl><description>Thirukannapuram. Perumal: Neelameghan; utsavar Sowrirajan. Thayar: Kannapura Nayaki. Posture: Standing. Kulasekhara Azhwar&apos;s lullaby to Sri Rama, &quot;Mannu pugazh Kosalai&quot;, is addressed to the Lord of this town.</description><ExtendedData><Data name="Number"><value>17</value></Data><Data name="Region"><value>Chola Nadu</value></Data><Data name="Tamil"><value>திருக்கண்ணபுரம்</value></Data></ExtendedData><Point><coordinates>79.7043,10.8685,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>18. Thirukkannangudi</name><styleUrl>#sCholaNadu</styleUrl><description>Thirukannangudi. Perumal: Lokanathan; utsavar Damodara Narayanan. Thayar: Lokanayaki (Aravindavalli). Posture: Standing. Krishna was bound here by the affection of sage Vasishtha. Many Thirumangai Azhwar stories are told about its tree, well and field.</description><ExtendedData><Data name="Number"><value>18</value></Data><Data name="Region"><value>Chola Nadu</value></Data><Data name="Tamil"><value>திருக்கண்ணங்குடி</value></Data></ExtendedData><Point><coordinates>79.7633,10.7572,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>19. Thirunagai</name><styleUrl>#sCholaNadu</styleUrl><description>Nagapattinam (Soundararaja Perumal). Perumal: Neelameghan; utsavar Soundararajan. Thayar: Soundaryavalli. Posture: Standing. Thirumangai Azhwar, speaking as a girl in love, can only repeat &quot;acho oruvar azhagiyava&quot;, what a beauty!</description><ExtendedData><Data name="Number"><value>19</value></Data><Data name="Region"><value>Chola Nadu</value></Data><Data name="Tamil"><value>திருநாகை</value></Data></ExtendedData><Point><coordinates>79.8437,10.7598,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>20. Thanjai Mamani Koil</name><styleUrl>#sCholaNadu</styleUrl><description>Thanjavur (three temples). Perumal: Neelameghan, Manikundran and Narasimhan. Thayar: Senkamalavalli, Ambujavalli, Thanjai Nayaki. Posture: Sitting. Three neighbouring temples are counted as one Divya Desam. The Lord ended the demon Tanjaka here, which gave Thanjavur its name.</description><ExtendedData><Data name="Number"><value>20</value></Data><Data name="Region"><value>Chola Nadu</value></Data><Data name="Tamil"><value>தஞ்சை மாமணிக்கோயில்</value></Data></ExtendedData><Point><coordinates>79.1387,10.8157,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>21. Thirunandipura Vinnagaram</name><styleUrl>#sCholaNadu</styleUrl><description>Nathan Koil. Perumal: Jagannathan (Nathanathan). Thayar: Shenbagavalli. Posture: Sitting. Nandi was freed from a curse here. The kshetram is also called Dakshina Jagannatham.</description><ExtendedData><Data name="Number"><value>21</value></Data><Data name="Region"><value>Chola Nadu</value></Data><Data name="Tamil"><value>திருநந்திபுரவிண்ணகரம்</value></Data></ExtendedData><Point><coordinates>79.3722,10.9221,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>22. Thiruvelliyangudi</name><styleUrl>#sCholaNadu</styleUrl><description>Thiruvelliyangudi. Perumal: Kolavalvilli Raman. Thayar: Maragathavalli. Posture: Reclining. Sukra (Velli) regained his sight here. Garuda in this temple uniquely holds the conch and discus.</description><ExtendedData><Data name="Number"><value>22</value></Data><Data name="Region"><value>Chola Nadu</value></Data><Data name="Tamil"><value>திருவெள்ளியங்குடி</value></Data></ExtendedData><Point><coordinates>79.4431,11.0567,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>23. Thiruvazhundur</name><styleUrl>#sCholaNadu</styleUrl><description>Therazhundur. Perumal: Devadirajan; utsavar Amaruviappan. Thayar: Senkamalavalli. Posture: Standing. Krishna stands as the cowherd Amaruviappan with a cow and calf. It is also the birthplace of the poet Kambar.</description><ExtendedData><Data name="Number"><value>23</value></Data><Data name="Region"><value>Chola Nadu</value></Data><Data name="Tamil"><value>திருவழுந்தூர்</value></Data></ExtendedData><Point><coordinates>79.5795,11.0465,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>24. Thiruchirupuliyur</name><styleUrl>#sCholaNadu</styleUrl><description>Sirupuliyur. Perumal: Arulmakadal (Kripasamudra Perumal). Thayar: Thirumamagal Nachiyar. Posture: Reclining. The Lord reclines here in a small, child-sized form (bala sayanam) at the request of sage Vyaghrapada.</description><ExtendedData><Data name="Number"><value>24</value></Data><Data name="Region"><value>Chola Nadu</value></Data><Data name="Tamil"><value>திருச்சிறுபுலியூர்</value></Data></ExtendedData><Point><coordinates>79.6694,10.9912,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>25. Thalaichanga Nanmadiyam</name><styleUrl>#sCholaNadu</styleUrl><description>Thalachangadu. Perumal: Nanmadiya Perumal; utsavar Venchudar Perumal. Thayar: Thalaichanga Nachiyar. Posture: Standing. Chandra, the moon, was relieved of his curse here, and the Lord wears the crescent.</description><ExtendedData><Data name="Number"><value>25</value></Data><Data name="Region"><value>Chola Nadu</value></Data><Data name="Tamil"><value>தலைச்சங்க நாண்மதியம்</value></Data></ExtendedData><Point><coordinates>79.7853,11.1298,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>26. Thiruvindalur</name><styleUrl>#sCholaNadu</styleUrl><description>Indalur, Mayiladuthurai (Parimala Ranganathar). Perumal: Parimala Ranganathan. Thayar: Parimala Ranganayaki. Posture: Reclining. A place of Ekadasi glory. Thirumangai Azhwar, finding the doors shut, scolds the Lord lovingly in his verses.</description><ExtendedData><Data name="Number"><value>26</value></Data><Data name="Region"><value>Chola Nadu</value></Data><Data name="Tamil"><value>திருஇந்தளூர்</value></Data></ExtendedData><Point><coordinates>79.6462,11.1097,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>27. Thirukkavalambadi</name><styleUrl>#sCholaNadu</styleUrl><description>Thirunangur (Gopalakrishnan). Perumal: Gopalakrishnan (Rajagopalan). Thayar: Madavaral Mangai, with Rukmini and Satyabhama. Posture: Standing. Krishna stands with Rukmini and Satyabhama. Tradition links the grove to the parijata He brought for Satyabhama.</description><ExtendedData><Data name="Number"><value>27</value></Data><Data name="Region"><value>Chola Nadu</value></Data><Data name="Tamil"><value>திருக்காவளம்பாடி</value></Data></ExtendedData><Point><coordinates>79.7824,11.1769,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>28. Kazhicheerama Vinnagaram</name><styleUrl>#sCholaNadu</styleUrl><description>Sirkazhi (Thadalan Koil). Perumal: Trivikraman (Thadalan). Thayar: Lokanayaki. Posture: Standing. Trivikrama stands with His left foot raised to measure the worlds. Thirumangai Azhwar won his spear in a poetry contest here.</description><ExtendedData><Data name="Number"><value>28</value></Data><Data name="Region"><value>Chola Nadu</value></Data><Data name="Tamil"><value>காழிச்சீராம விண்ணகரம்</value></Data></ExtendedData><Point><coordinates>79.7317,11.241,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>29. Arimeya Vinnagaram</name><styleUrl>#sCholaNadu</styleUrl><description>Thirunangur (Kudamadu Koothan). Perumal: Kudamadu Koothan. Thayar: Amritaghatavalli. Posture: Sitting. Krishna, the dancer with the pots. Sung as the One who lifted Govardhana.</description><ExtendedData><Data name="Number"><value>29</value></Data><Data name="Region"><value>Chola Nadu</value></Data><Data name="Tamil"><value>அரிமேய விண்ணகரம்</value></Data></ExtendedData><Point><coordinates>79.7815,11.1777,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>30. Vanpurushottamam</name><styleUrl>#sCholaNadu</styleUrl><description>Thirunangur (Purushottaman). Perumal: Purushottaman. Thayar: Purushottama Nayaki. Posture: Standing. The Lord gave an ocean of milk to the hungry child Upamanyu here. Associated with Rama of Ayodhya among the Nangur eleven.</description><ExtendedData><Data name="Number"><value>30</value></Data><Data name="Region"><value>Chola Nadu</value></Data><Data name="Tamil"><value>வண்புருடோத்தமம்</value></Data></ExtendedData><Point><coordinates>79.7767,11.1788,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>31. Semponsei Koil</name><styleUrl>#sCholaNadu</styleUrl><description>Thirunangur (Perarulalan). Perumal: Perarulalan. Thayar: Allimamalar Nachiyar. Posture: Standing. Named &quot;the temple made of pure gold&quot;. Sri Rama is said to have gifted a golden cow here after the war.</description><ExtendedData><Data name="Number"><value>31</value></Data><Data name="Region"><value>Chola Nadu</value></Data><Data name="Tamil"><value>செம்பொன்செய்கோயில்</value></Data></ExtendedData><Point><coordinates>79.7797,11.1784,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>32. Manimada Koil</name><styleUrl>#sCholaNadu</styleUrl><description>Thirunangur (Narayana Perumal). Perumal: Narayanan (Nanda Vilakku). Thayar: Pundarikavalli. Posture: Sitting. The eleven Perumals of Nangur assemble here on Garuda the day after Thai Amavasya, with Thirumangai Azhwar greeting each one.</description><ExtendedData><Data name="Number"><value>32</value></Data><Data name="Region"><value>Chola Nadu</value></Data><Data name="Tamil"><value>மணிமாடக்கோயில்</value></Data></ExtendedData><Point><coordinates>79.7769,11.174,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>33. Vaikunta Vinnagaram</name><styleUrl>#sCholaNadu</styleUrl><description>Thirunangur (Vaikuntanathan). Perumal: Vaikuntanathan. Thayar: Vaikuntavalli. Posture: Sitting. The Lord sits as in Paramapadam, with Sri, Bhu and Nila.</description><ExtendedData><Data name="Number"><value>33</value></Data><Data name="Region"><value>Chola Nadu</value></Data><Data name="Tamil"><value>வைகுந்த விண்ணகரம்</value></Data></ExtendedData><Point><coordinates>79.7783,11.1798,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>34. Thiruvali Thirunagari</name><styleUrl>#sCholaNadu</styleUrl><description>Thiruvali and Thirunagari. Perumal: Lakshmi Narasimhan (Thiruvali); Vedarajan (Thirunagari). Thayar: Amritaghatavalli; Amritavalli. Posture: Sitting. Twin temples counted as one. Thirumangai Azhwar tried to rob a wedding party here, and the Bridegroom gave him the eight-syllable mantra instead.</description><ExtendedData><Data name="Number"><value>34</value></Data><Data name="Region"><value>Chola Nadu</value></Data><Data name="Tamil"><value>திருவாலி திருநகரி</value></Data></ExtendedData><Point><coordinates>79.7745,11.203,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>35. Thiruthevanar Thogai</name><styleUrl>#sCholaNadu</styleUrl><description>Thirunangur (Madhava Perumal), Keezhachalai. Perumal: Deivanayakan; utsavar Madhava Perumal. Thayar: Kadalmagal Nachiyar. Posture: Standing. The devas gathered here in a crowd (thogai) to see the Lord&apos;s wedding with the daughter of the ocean.</description><ExtendedData><Data name="Number"><value>35</value></Data><Data name="Region"><value>Chola Nadu</value></Data><Data name="Tamil"><value>திருத்தேவனார்தொகை</value></Data></ExtendedData><Point><coordinates>79.7755,11.1968,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>36. Thiruthetriambalam</name><styleUrl>#sCholaNadu</styleUrl><description>Thirunangur (Palli Konda Perumal). Perumal: Senganmal (Lakshmi Rangar). Thayar: Senkamalavalli. Posture: Reclining. The only one of the eleven Nangur temples where the Lord reclines, and the only Divya Desam called an ambalam.</description><ExtendedData><Data name="Number"><value>36</value></Data><Data name="Region"><value>Chola Nadu</value></Data><Data name="Tamil"><value>திருத்தெற்றியம்பலம்</value></Data></ExtendedData><Point><coordinates>79.7951,11.173,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>37. Thirumanikkoodam</name><styleUrl>#sCholaNadu</styleUrl><description>Thirunangur (Varadaraja Perumal). Perumal: Varadarajan (Manikkooda Nayakan). Thayar: Thirumamagal Nachiyar. Posture: Standing. Linked with Varadaraja of Kanchi among the Nangur eleven. Chandra worshipped here.</description><ExtendedData><Data name="Number"><value>37</value></Data><Data name="Region"><value>Chola Nadu</value></Data><Data name="Tamil"><value>திருமணிக்கூடம்</value></Data></ExtendedData><Point><coordinates>79.7778,11.1774,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>38. Thiruvellakkulam</name><styleUrl>#sCholaNadu</styleUrl><description>Annan Koil, Thirunangur. Perumal: Srinivasan (Annan Perumal). Thayar: Alarmel Mangai. Posture: Standing. Called the elder brother (Annan) of Tirumala&apos;s Lord. Kumudavalli, who turned Thirumangai Azhwar to devotion, appeared here.</description><ExtendedData><Data name="Number"><value>38</value></Data><Data name="Region"><value>Chola Nadu</value></Data><Data name="Tamil"><value>திருவெள்ளக்குளம்</value></Data></ExtendedData><Point><coordinates>79.7649,11.1901,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>39. Thirupparthanpalli</name><styleUrl>#sCholaNadu</styleUrl><description>Parthanpalli. Perumal: Thamaraiyal Kelvan; utsavar Parthasarathy. Thayar: Thamarai Nayaki. Posture: Standing. Krishna taught and comforted Arjuna (Partha) here, and brought forth water for him.</description><ExtendedData><Data name="Number"><value>39</value></Data><Data name="Region"><value>Chola Nadu</value></Data><Data name="Tamil"><value>திருப்பார்த்தன்பள்ளி</value></Data></ExtendedData><Point><coordinates>79.7975,11.17,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>40. Thiruchitrakoodam</name><styleUrl>#sCholaNadu</styleUrl><description>Chidambaram (Govindaraja Perumal). Perumal: Govindarajan. Thayar: Pundarikavalli. Posture: Reclining. The Lord reclines inside the great Nataraja temple, watching the cosmic dance. Kulasekhara Azhwar tells the whole Ramayana in his decad on this shrine.</description><ExtendedData><Data name="Number"><value>40</value></Data><Data name="Region"><value>Chola Nadu</value></Data><Data name="Tamil"><value>திருச்சித்ரகூடம்</value></Data></ExtendedData><Point><coordinates>79.6934,11.3992,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark></Folder>
<Folder><name>Nadu Nadu</name><Placemark><name>41. Thiruvahindrapuram</name><styleUrl>#sNaduNadu</styleUrl><description>Thiruvanthipuram, near Cuddalore. Perumal: Devanathan. Thayar: Hemambujavalli (Vaikunta Nayaki). Posture: Standing. Vedanta Desika meditated on the Oushadagiri hillock here and received the grace of Hayagriva and Garuda.</description><ExtendedData><Data name="Number"><value>41</value></Data><Data name="Region"><value>Nadu Nadu</value></Data><Data name="Tamil"><value>திருவஹீந்திரபுரம்</value></Data></ExtendedData><Point><coordinates>79.7094,11.7451,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>42. Thirukkovalur</name><styleUrl>#sNaduNadu</styleUrl><description>Thirukoilur (Ulagalantha Perumal). Perumal: Trivikraman; utsavar Ayanar (Gopalan). Thayar: Poongoval Nachiyar. Posture: Standing. The three first Azhwars met in a narrow passage on a stormy night, felt a fourth Person pressing among them, and the Divya Prabandham was born.</description><ExtendedData><Data name="Number"><value>42</value></Data><Data name="Region"><value>Nadu Nadu</value></Data><Data name="Tamil"><value>திருக்கோவலூர்</value></Data></ExtendedData><Point><coordinates>79.2025,11.967,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark></Folder>
<Folder><name>Thondai Nadu</name><Placemark><name>43. Thirukkachi Atthigiri</name><styleUrl>#sThondaiNadu</styleUrl><description>Kanchipuram (Varadaraja Perumal). Perumal: Varadarajan (Devaraja, Perarulalan). Thayar: Perundevi. Posture: Standing. Perumal Koil, where Ramanuja served daily and Thirukachi Nambi fanned the Lord. Athi Varadar, the fig-wood form, is brought out of the tank once in forty years.</description><ExtendedData><Data name="Number"><value>43</value></Data><Data name="Region"><value>Thondai Nadu</value></Data><Data name="Tamil"><value>திருக்கச்சி அத்திகிரி</value></Data></ExtendedData><Point><coordinates>79.7246,12.8191,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>44. Ashtabuyagaram</name><styleUrl>#sThondaiNadu</styleUrl><description>Kanchipuram (Ashtabhuja Perumal). Perumal: Adikesavan (Ashtabhuja Perumal). Thayar: Alarmelmangai (Padmasani). Posture: Standing. The Lord stands with eight arms and eight weapons, come to protect Brahma&apos;s sacrifice.</description><ExtendedData><Data name="Number"><value>44</value></Data><Data name="Region"><value>Thondai Nadu</value></Data><Data name="Tamil"><value>அட்டபுயகரம்</value></Data></ExtendedData><Point><coordinates>79.7108,12.8227,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>45. Thiruthanka</name><styleUrl>#sThondaiNadu</styleUrl><description>Thoopul, Kanchipuram (Vilakkoli Perumal). Perumal: Deepaprakasan (Vilakkoli Perumal). Thayar: Maragathavalli. Posture: Standing. The Lord appeared as a light to dispel darkness at Brahma&apos;s sacrifice. Vedanta Desika was born next door at Thoopul.</description><ExtendedData><Data name="Number"><value>45</value></Data><Data name="Region"><value>Thondai Nadu</value></Data><Data name="Tamil"><value>திருத்தண்கா</value></Data></ExtendedData><Point><coordinates>79.7055,12.8244,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>46. Thiruvelukkai</name><styleUrl>#sThondaiNadu</styleUrl><description>Kanchipuram (Azhagiya Singar). Perumal: Azhagiya Singar (Mukunda Nayakan). Thayar: Velukkai Valli (Amritavalli). Posture: Sitting. Narasimha chose to stay (vel irukkai, the place He wished to stay) after driving away the demons.</description><ExtendedData><Data name="Number"><value>46</value></Data><Data name="Region"><value>Thondai Nadu</value></Data><Data name="Tamil"><value>திருவேளுக்கை</value></Data></ExtendedData><Point><coordinates>79.7065,12.8222,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>47. Thiruneeragam</name><styleUrl>#sThondaiNadu</styleUrl><description>Kanchipuram (inside Ulagalantha Perumal temple). Perumal: Jagadisvaran (Neeragathan). Thayar: Nilamangai Valli. Posture: Standing. One of four Divya Desams inside the Ulagalantha Perumal compound, sung in a single shared verse.</description><ExtendedData><Data name="Number"><value>47</value></Data><Data name="Region"><value>Thondai Nadu</value></Data><Data name="Tamil"><value>திருநீரகம்</value></Data></ExtendedData><Point><coordinates>79.7052,12.8391,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>48. Thiruppadagam</name><styleUrl>#sThondaiNadu</styleUrl><description>Kanchipuram (Pandava Thoothar). Perumal: Pandava Thoothar. Thayar: Rukmini, Satyabhama. Posture: Sitting. A towering seated Krishna, showing the universal form He revealed in the Kaurava court as the Pandavas&apos; messenger.</description><ExtendedData><Data name="Number"><value>48</value></Data><Data name="Region"><value>Thondai Nadu</value></Data><Data name="Tamil"><value>திருப்பாடகம்</value></Data></ExtendedData><Point><coordinates>79.6969,12.8427,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>49. Nilathingal Thundam</name><styleUrl>#sThondaiNadu</styleUrl><description>Kanchipuram (inside Ekambareswarar temple). Perumal: Nilathingal Thundathan. Thayar: Nervoruvar Illa Valli. Posture: Standing. A Divya Desam inside a Shiva temple, where the Lord cooled Parvati&apos;s penance with moonlight.</description><ExtendedData><Data name="Number"><value>49</value></Data><Data name="Region"><value>Thondai Nadu</value></Data><Data name="Tamil"><value>நிலாத்திங்கள் துண்டம்</value></Data></ExtendedData><Point><coordinates>79.6993,12.8475,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>50. Thiruooragam</name><styleUrl>#sThondaiNadu</styleUrl><description>Kanchipuram (Ulagalantha Perumal). Perumal: Ulagalantha Perumal (Trivikraman); Uragathan. Thayar: Amudavalli (Amritavalli). Posture: Standing. A Trivikrama about 35 feet tall. He also gives darshan as a serpent (uraga) for Mahabali, who could not take in the huge form.</description><ExtendedData><Data name="Number"><value>50</value></Data><Data name="Region"><value>Thondai Nadu</value></Data><Data name="Tamil"><value>திருஊரகம்</value></Data></ExtendedData><Point><coordinates>79.7052,12.8391,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>51. Thiruvekka</name><styleUrl>#sThondaiNadu</styleUrl><description>Kanchipuram (Yathothakari, Sonna Vannam Seitha Perumal). Perumal: Yathothakari. Thayar: Komalavalli. Posture: Reclining. &quot;The Lord who did as He was told.&quot; He rolled up His serpent bed and followed Thirumazhisai Azhwar out of the city, then came back and lay down the other way round.</description><ExtendedData><Data name="Number"><value>51</value></Data><Data name="Region"><value>Thondai Nadu</value></Data><Data name="Tamil"><value>திருவெஃகா</value></Data></ExtendedData><Point><coordinates>79.7125,12.8241,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>52. Thirukkaragam</name><styleUrl>#sThondaiNadu</styleUrl><description>Kanchipuram (inside Ulagalantha Perumal temple). Perumal: Karunakaran. Thayar: Padmamani Nachiyar. Posture: Standing. Within the Ulagalantha Perumal compound, named in the same single verse as Neeragam and Karvanam.</description><ExtendedData><Data name="Number"><value>52</value></Data><Data name="Region"><value>Thondai Nadu</value></Data><Data name="Tamil"><value>திருக்காரகம்</value></Data></ExtendedData><Point><coordinates>79.7052,12.8391,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>53. Thirukkarvanam</name><styleUrl>#sThondaiNadu</styleUrl><description>Kanchipuram (inside Ulagalantha Perumal temple). Perumal: Kalvar (Navaneeta Choran). Thayar: Kamalavalli. Posture: Standing. The Lord the colour of a rain cloud, in the Ulagalantha Perumal compound.</description><ExtendedData><Data name="Number"><value>53</value></Data><Data name="Region"><value>Thondai Nadu</value></Data><Data name="Tamil"><value>திருக்கார்வானம்</value></Data></ExtendedData><Point><coordinates>79.7052,12.8391,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>54. Thirukkalvanur</name><styleUrl>#sThondaiNadu</styleUrl><description>Kanchipuram (inside Kamakshi Amman temple). Perumal: Adi Varahan (Kalvar). Thayar: Anjilai Valli. Posture: Standing. A small shrine inside the Kamakshi temple. The Lord is the &quot;thief&quot; who overheard a conversation between Lakshmi and Parvati.</description><ExtendedData><Data name="Number"><value>54</value></Data><Data name="Region"><value>Thondai Nadu</value></Data><Data name="Tamil"><value>திருக்கள்வனூர்</value></Data></ExtendedData><Point><coordinates>79.7032,12.8407,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>55. Thiruppavalavannam</name><styleUrl>#sThondaiNadu</styleUrl><description>Kanchipuram (Pavalavannar). Perumal: Pavalavannan. Thayar: Pavalavalli. Posture: Standing. The coral-coloured Lord. Pilgrims pair it with the emerald Pachaivannar temple opposite.</description><ExtendedData><Data name="Number"><value>55</value></Data><Data name="Region"><value>Thondai Nadu</value></Data><Data name="Tamil"><value>திருப்பவளவண்ணம்</value></Data></ExtendedData><Point><coordinates>79.7076,12.8437,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>56. Parameswara Vinnagaram</name><styleUrl>#sThondaiNadu</styleUrl><description>Kanchipuram (Vaikunta Perumal). Perumal: Paramapadanathan (Vaikuntanathan). Thayar: Vaikuntavalli. Posture: Sitting, Reclining, Standing. A Pallava temple of three storeys, with the Lord sitting, reclining and standing one above another.</description><ExtendedData><Data name="Number"><value>56</value></Data><Data name="Region"><value>Thondai Nadu</value></Data><Data name="Tamil"><value>பரமேச்சுர விண்ணகரம்</value></Data></ExtendedData><Point><coordinates>79.7095,12.8372,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>57. Thirupputkuzhi</name><styleUrl>#sThondaiNadu</styleUrl><description>Thiruputkuzhi. Perumal: Vijayaraghavan. Thayar: Maragathavalli. Posture: Sitting. Sri Rama sits holding Jatayu, having performed the bird&apos;s last rites here. Ramanuja studied in this village as a boy.</description><ExtendedData><Data name="Number"><value>57</value></Data><Data name="Region"><value>Thondai Nadu</value></Data><Data name="Tamil"><value>திருப்புட்குழி</value></Data></ExtendedData><Point><coordinates>79.6187,12.8726,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>58. Thirunindravur</name><styleUrl>#sThondaiNadu</styleUrl><description>Thirunindravur (Bhaktavatsala Perumal). Perumal: Bhaktavatsalan (Pathavatsalan). Thayar: Ennai Petra Thayar (Sudhavalli). Posture: Standing. Thayar is called &quot;the Mother who bore me&quot;. Tradition says She sent the Lord after Thirumangai Azhwar to obtain a verse.</description><ExtendedData><Data name="Number"><value>58</value></Data><Data name="Region"><value>Thondai Nadu</value></Data><Data name="Tamil"><value>திருநின்றவூர்</value></Data></ExtendedData><Point><coordinates>80.0261,13.1125,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>59. Thiruevvul</name><styleUrl>#sThondaiNadu</styleUrl><description>Tiruvallur (Veeraraghava Perumal). Perumal: Veeraraghavan (Vaidya Veeraraghavan). Thayar: Kanakavalli. Posture: Reclining. The Lord asked sage Salihotra &quot;evvul?&quot;, in which room may I rest. Pilgrims pray here for healing, especially on new moon days.</description><ExtendedData><Data name="Number"><value>59</value></Data><Data name="Region"><value>Thondai Nadu</value></Data><Data name="Tamil"><value>திருஎவ்வுள்</value></Data></ExtendedData><Point><coordinates>79.9074,13.1432,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>60. Thiruvallikkeni</name><styleUrl>#sThondaiNadu</styleUrl><description>Triplicane, Chennai (Parthasarathy). Perumal: Venkatakrishnan; utsavar Parthasarathy. Thayar: Rukmini; Vedavalli. Posture: Standing. Krishna as Arjuna&apos;s charioteer, with a moustache and without the discus. The utsavar&apos;s face bears the marks of Bhishma&apos;s arrows.</description><ExtendedData><Data name="Number"><value>60</value></Data><Data name="Region"><value>Thondai Nadu</value></Data><Data name="Tamil"><value>திருவல்லிக்கேணி</value></Data></ExtendedData><Point><coordinates>80.2769,13.0539,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>61. Thiruneermalai</name><styleUrl>#sThondaiNadu</styleUrl><description>Thiruneermalai, near Pallavaram. Perumal: Neervannan; Ranganathan; Santa Narasimhan; Trivikraman. Thayar: Animamalar Mangai; Ranganayaki. Posture: Standing, Sitting, Reclining, Striding. The one place to see the Lord standing, sitting, reclining and striding, at the foot and on top of a small hill.</description><ExtendedData><Data name="Number"><value>61</value></Data><Data name="Region"><value>Thondai Nadu</value></Data><Data name="Tamil"><value>திருநீர்மலை</value></Data></ExtendedData><Point><coordinates>80.115,12.9638,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>62. Thiruvidanthai</name><styleUrl>#sThondaiNadu</styleUrl><description>Thiruvidanthai, East Coast Road (Nitya Kalyana Perumal). Perumal: Lakshmi Varahan; utsavar Nitya Kalyana Perumal. Thayar: Komalavalli (Akhilavalli). Posture: Standing. Varaha holds Bhumi Devi on His left side. The Lord married 360 maidens here, one each day, so every day is a wedding day.</description><ExtendedData><Data name="Number"><value>62</value></Data><Data name="Region"><value>Thondai Nadu</value></Data><Data name="Tamil"><value>திருவிடவெந்தை</value></Data></ExtendedData><Point><coordinates>80.2425,12.7632,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>63. Thirukkadalmallai</name><styleUrl>#sThondaiNadu</styleUrl><description>Mamallapuram (Sthalasayana Perumal). Perumal: Sthalasayana Perumal. Thayar: Nilamangai Nachiyar. Posture: Reclining. The Lord lies on the bare ground without Adisesha, having come to sage Pundarika. Birthplace of Bhoothath Azhwar.</description><ExtendedData><Data name="Number"><value>63</value></Data><Data name="Region"><value>Thondai Nadu</value></Data><Data name="Tamil"><value>திருக்கடல்மல்லை</value></Data></ExtendedData><Point><coordinates>80.1933,12.6175,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>64. Thirukkadigai</name><styleUrl>#sThondaiNadu</styleUrl><description>Sholinghur (Yoga Narasimha). Perumal: Yoga Narasimhan (Akkarakkani). Thayar: Amritavalli. Posture: Sitting. Staying here for one kadigai, about 24 minutes, is said to be enough. Yoga Narasimha is on the big hill and Yoga Anjaneya on the small hill.</description><ExtendedData><Data name="Number"><value>64</value></Data><Data name="Region"><value>Thondai Nadu</value></Data><Data name="Tamil"><value>திருக்கடிகை</value></Data></ExtendedData><Point><coordinates>79.4246,13.0937,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark></Folder>
<Folder><name>Malai Nadu</name><Placemark><name>65. Thirunavai</name><styleUrl>#sMalaiNadu</styleUrl><description>Tirunavaya (Navamukunda). Perumal: Navamukundan (Narayanan). Thayar: Malarmangai Nachiyar. Posture: Standing. On the bank of the Bharathapuzha. Unusually for Kerala, the Goddess has Her own separate shrine.</description><ExtendedData><Data name="Number"><value>65</value></Data><Data name="Region"><value>Malai Nadu</value></Data><Data name="Tamil"><value>திருநாவாய்</value></Data></ExtendedData><Point><coordinates>76.8365,10.3607,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>66. Thiruvithuvakkodu</name><styleUrl>#sMalaiNadu</styleUrl><description>Thirumittakode, near Pattambi. Perumal: Uyyavantha Perumal (Abhayapradan). Thayar: Vithuvakkottuvalli (Padmasani). Posture: Standing. Kulasekhara Azhwar&apos;s decad of ten similes of helpless dependence, such as the child who clings to the mother even when she pushes it away.</description><ExtendedData><Data name="Number"><value>66</value></Data><Data name="Region"><value>Malai Nadu</value></Data><Data name="Tamil"><value>திருவித்துவக்கோடு</value></Data></ExtendedData><Point><coordinates>76.8365,10.3607,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>67. Thirukkatkarai</name><styleUrl>#sMalaiNadu</styleUrl><description>Thrikkakara, Kochi (Vamana Murti). Perumal: Katkarai Appan (Vamana). Thayar: Perunchelva Nayaki (Vatsalyavalli). Posture: Standing. The seat of the Onam festival, where Vamana received three paces of land from Mahabali.</description><ExtendedData><Data name="Number"><value>67</value></Data><Data name="Region"><value>Malai Nadu</value></Data><Data name="Tamil"><value>திருக்காட்கரை</value></Data></ExtendedData><Point><coordinates>76.8365,10.3607,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>68. Thirumoozhikkalam</name><styleUrl>#sMalaiNadu</styleUrl><description>Thirumoozhikulam (Lakshmana Perumal). Perumal: Thirumoozhikkalathan (Lakshmana Perumal). Thayar: Madhuraveni Nachiyar. Posture: Standing. Worshipped as Lakshmana in Kerala&apos;s Nalambalam circuit of the four brothers of Sri Rama.</description><ExtendedData><Data name="Number"><value>68</value></Data><Data name="Region"><value>Malai Nadu</value></Data><Data name="Tamil"><value>திருமூழிக்களம்</value></Data></ExtendedData><Point><coordinates>76.8365,10.3607,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>69. Thiruvallavazh</name><styleUrl>#sMalaiNadu</styleUrl><description>Thiruvalla (Sri Vallabha). Perumal: Kolappiran (Sri Vallabhan). Thayar: Selva Thirukkozhundu Nachiyar (Vatsalya Devi). Posture: Standing. Known for daily Kathakali offered as worship, and for a tall granite flagstaff topped by Garuda.</description><ExtendedData><Data name="Number"><value>69</value></Data><Data name="Region"><value>Malai Nadu</value></Data><Data name="Tamil"><value>திருவல்லவாழ்</value></Data></ExtendedData><Point><coordinates>76.8173,9.4272,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>70. Thirukkadithanam</name><styleUrl>#sMalaiNadu</styleUrl><description>Thrikkodithanam. Perumal: Arputha Narayanan (Amrita Narayanan). Thayar: Karpagavalli. Posture: Standing. One of the five temples linked to the Pandavas, this one to Sahadeva.</description><ExtendedData><Data name="Number"><value>70</value></Data><Data name="Region"><value>Malai Nadu</value></Data><Data name="Tamil"><value>திருக்கடித்தானம்</value></Data></ExtendedData><Point><coordinates>76.8173,9.4272,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>71. Thiruchenkundrur</name><styleUrl>#sMalaiNadu</styleUrl><description>Thrichittattu, Chengannur. Perumal: Imayavarappan. Thayar: Senkamalavalli. Posture: Standing. Linked to Yudhishthira, who is said to have prayed here after the war for having spoken a half-truth.</description><ExtendedData><Data name="Number"><value>71</value></Data><Data name="Region"><value>Malai Nadu</value></Data><Data name="Tamil"><value>திருச்செங்குன்றூர்</value></Data></ExtendedData><Point><coordinates>76.8173,9.4272,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>72. Thiruppuliyur</name><styleUrl>#sMalaiNadu</styleUrl><description>Thripuliyur, near Chengannur. Perumal: Mayapiran. Thayar: Porkodi Nachiyar. Posture: Standing. Linked to Bhima. Nammazhwar speaks as the friend of a girl who is already wholly given to Mayapiran.</description><ExtendedData><Data name="Number"><value>72</value></Data><Data name="Region"><value>Malai Nadu</value></Data><Data name="Tamil"><value>திருப்புலியூர்</value></Data></ExtendedData><Point><coordinates>76.8173,9.4272,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>73. Thiruvaranvilai</name><styleUrl>#sMalaiNadu</styleUrl><description>Aranmula (Parthasarathy). Perumal: Thirukkuralappan (Parthasarathy). Thayar: Padmasani Nachiyar. Posture: Standing. Linked to Arjuna. Famous for the Pampa snake boat race and the Aranmula metal mirror.</description><ExtendedData><Data name="Number"><value>73</value></Data><Data name="Region"><value>Malai Nadu</value></Data><Data name="Tamil"><value>திருவாறன்விளை</value></Data></ExtendedData><Point><coordinates>76.7603,9.3554,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>74. Thiruvanvandoor</name><styleUrl>#sMalaiNadu</styleUrl><description>Thiruvanvandoor, near Chengannur. Perumal: Pambanai Appan (Kamalanathan). Thayar: Kamalavalli Nachiyar. Posture: Standing. Linked to Nakula. Nammazhwar sends birds as messengers to the Lord in this decad.</description><ExtendedData><Data name="Number"><value>74</value></Data><Data name="Region"><value>Malai Nadu</value></Data><Data name="Tamil"><value>திருவண்வண்டூர்</value></Data></ExtendedData><Point><coordinates>76.7603,9.3554,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>75. Thiruvananthapuram</name><styleUrl>#sMalaiNadu</styleUrl><description>Sri Padmanabhaswamy Temple. Perumal: Anantha Padmanabhan. Thayar: Sri Hari Lakshmi. Posture: Reclining. The Lord is so long that He is seen through three doors: face, navel and feet. Sri Caitanya Mahaprabhu had darshan here.</description><ExtendedData><Data name="Number"><value>75</value></Data><Data name="Region"><value>Malai Nadu</value></Data><Data name="Tamil"><value>திருவனந்தபுரம்</value></Data></ExtendedData><Point><coordinates>76.9279,8.534,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>76. Thiruvattaru</name><styleUrl>#sMalaiNadu</styleUrl><description>Thiruvattar (Adikesava Perumal). Perumal: Adikesavan. Thayar: Maragathavalli. Posture: Reclining. Regarded as the elder of the two great reclining forms of the far south. Sri Caitanya Mahaprabhu found the Brahma-samhita in this temple.</description><ExtendedData><Data name="Number"><value>76</value></Data><Data name="Region"><value>Malai Nadu</value></Data><Data name="Tamil"><value>திருவட்டாறு</value></Data></ExtendedData><Point><coordinates>77.2417,8.369,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>77. Thiruvanparisaram</name><styleUrl>#sMalaiNadu</styleUrl><description>Thiruppathisaram, near Nagercoil. Perumal: Thiruvazhmarban (Thirukkuralappan). Thayar: Kamalavalli Nachiyar. Posture: Sitting. The home village of Udayanangai, mother of Nammazhwar. Lakshmi dwells on the Lord&apos;s chest, so there is no separate Thayar shrine.</description><ExtendedData><Data name="Number"><value>77</value></Data><Data name="Region"><value>Malai Nadu</value></Data><Data name="Tamil"><value>திருவண்பரிசாரம்</value></Data></ExtendedData><Point><coordinates>77.4703,8.2542,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark></Folder>
<Folder><name>Pandya Nadu</name><Placemark><name>78. Thirukkurungudi</name><styleUrl>#sPandyaNadu</styleUrl><description>Thirukkurungudi (Nambi Koil). Perumal: Sundara Paripooranan (Vaishnava Nambi): Nindra, Irundha and Kidantha Nambi. Thayar: Kurungudivalli Nachiyar. Posture: Standing, Sitting, Reclining. The Lord of this town is said to have been born as Nammazhwar. Home of the Kaisika Ekadasi story of Nampaduvan, and where Thirumangai Azhwar spent his last days.</description><ExtendedData><Data name="Number"><value>78</value></Data><Data name="Region"><value>Pandya Nadu</value></Data><Data name="Tamil"><value>திருக்குறுங்குடி</value></Data></ExtendedData><Point><coordinates>77.5259,8.4369,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>79. Thirucheeravaramangai</name><styleUrl>#sPandyaNadu</styleUrl><description>Nanguneri (Vanamamalai, Thotadri). Perumal: Thothadrinathan (Deivanayakan, Vanamamalai). Thayar: Srivaramangai Nachiyar. Posture: Sitting. A self-manifest kshetram and seat of the Vanamamalai Mutt. The oil from the Lord&apos;s daily abhishekam is collected in a well and taken as medicine.</description><ExtendedData><Data name="Number"><value>79</value></Data><Data name="Region"><value>Pandya Nadu</value></Data><Data name="Tamil"><value>திருச்சீரிவரமங்கை</value></Data></ExtendedData><Point><coordinates>77.5259,8.4369,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>80. Thiruvaikuntam</name><styleUrl>#sPandyaNadu</styleUrl><description>Srivaikuntam. Perumal: Vaikuntanathan; utsavar Kallappiran. Thayar: Vaikuntavalli. Posture: Standing. First of the Nava Tirupati on the Tamraparni (Surya). The sun&apos;s rays fall on the Lord on two days each year.</description><ExtendedData><Data name="Number"><value>80</value></Data><Data name="Region"><value>Pandya Nadu</value></Data><Data name="Tamil"><value>திருவைகுண்டம்</value></Data></ExtendedData><Point><coordinates>77.976,8.6097,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>81. Thiruvaragunamangai</name><styleUrl>#sPandyaNadu</styleUrl><description>Natham. Perumal: Vijayasana Perumal. Thayar: Varagunavalli. Posture: Sitting. Nava Tirupati (Chandra). The Lord sits under the hood of Adisesha.</description><ExtendedData><Data name="Number"><value>81</value></Data><Data name="Region"><value>Pandya Nadu</value></Data><Data name="Tamil"><value>திருவரகுணமங்கை</value></Data></ExtendedData><Point><coordinates>77.976,8.6097,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>82. Thiruppulingudi</name><styleUrl>#sPandyaNadu</styleUrl><description>Thirupulingudi. Perumal: Kaisina Vendan (Bhumipalan). Thayar: Malarmagal Nachiyar. Posture: Reclining. Nava Tirupati (Budha). The Lord&apos;s feet are seen through a window in the outer wall of the sanctum.</description><ExtendedData><Data name="Number"><value>82</value></Data><Data name="Region"><value>Pandya Nadu</value></Data><Data name="Tamil"><value>திருப்புளிங்குடி</value></Data></ExtendedData><Point><coordinates>77.976,8.6097,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>83. Tholaivillimangalam</name><styleUrl>#sPandyaNadu</styleUrl><description>Irattai Tirupati (twin temples). Perumal: Srinivasan (Devapiran); Aravindalochanan. Thayar: Karunthadankanni Nachiyar. Posture: Standing, Sitting. Two temples a short walk apart counted as one Divya Desam (Rahu and Ketu). Nammazhwar sings as a mother whose daughter cannot stop gazing towards this place.</description><ExtendedData><Data name="Number"><value>83</value></Data><Data name="Region"><value>Pandya Nadu</value></Data><Data name="Tamil"><value>தொலைவில்லிமங்கலம்</value></Data></ExtendedData><Point><coordinates>77.976,8.6097,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>84. Thirukkulanthai</name><styleUrl>#sPandyaNadu</styleUrl><description>Perungulam. Perumal: Srinivasan; utsavar Mayakkoothan. Thayar: Alarmelmangai (Kulandaivalli). Posture: Standing. Nava Tirupati (Sani). The Lord danced on the demon He defeated, hence Mayakkoothan.</description><ExtendedData><Data name="Number"><value>84</value></Data><Data name="Region"><value>Pandya Nadu</value></Data><Data name="Tamil"><value>திருக்குளந்தை</value></Data></ExtendedData><Point><coordinates>77.9505,8.607,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>85. Thirukkolur</name><styleUrl>#sPandyaNadu</styleUrl><description>Thirukkolur. Perumal: Vaithamanidhi Perumal. Thayar: Kumudavalli, Kolurvalli. Posture: Reclining. Birthplace of Madhurakavi Azhwar (Sevvai). The Lord rests on a grain measure, guarding Kubera&apos;s lost treasure.</description><ExtendedData><Data name="Number"><value>85</value></Data><Data name="Region"><value>Pandya Nadu</value></Data><Data name="Tamil"><value>திருக்கோளூர்</value></Data></ExtendedData><Point><coordinates>77.9739,8.6065,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>86. Thirupperai</name><styleUrl>#sPandyaNadu</styleUrl><description>Thenthirupperai. Perumal: Makara Nedunkuzhai Kathan. Thayar: Kuzhaikkathuvalli Nachiyar. Posture: Sitting. Nava Tirupati (Sukra). The Lord wears long fish-shaped earrings. Garuda&apos;s shrine is set aside so the Lord can watch children at play.</description><ExtendedData><Data name="Number"><value>86</value></Data><Data name="Region"><value>Pandya Nadu</value></Data><Data name="Tamil"><value>திருப்பேரை</value></Data></ExtendedData><Point><coordinates>77.9739,8.6065,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>87. Thirukkurugur</name><styleUrl>#sPandyaNadu</styleUrl><description>Azhwar Thirunagari. Perumal: Adinathan (Polindu Nindra Piran). Thayar: Adinathavalli, Kurugurvalli. Posture: Standing. Birthplace of Nammazhwar (Guru). The tamarind tree under which he sat in silence for sixteen years still stands in the temple.</description><ExtendedData><Data name="Number"><value>87</value></Data><Data name="Region"><value>Pandya Nadu</value></Data><Data name="Tamil"><value>திருக்குருகூர்</value></Data></ExtendedData><Point><coordinates>77.9505,8.607,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>88. Srivilliputhur</name><styleUrl>#sPandyaNadu</styleUrl><description>Srivilliputhur (Andal, Vatapatrasayi). Perumal: Vatapatrasayi; Rangamannar. Thayar: Andal (Kodai). Posture: Reclining. Home of Periyazhwar and his daughter Andal, the only woman among the Azhwars. The garland she wears is sent to Tirumala and Azhagar Koil each year.</description><ExtendedData><Data name="Number"><value>88</value></Data><Data name="Region"><value>Pandya Nadu</value></Data><Data name="Tamil"><value>ஸ்ரீவில்லிபுத்தூர்</value></Data></ExtendedData><Point><coordinates>77.9505,8.607,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>89. Thiruthangal</name><styleUrl>#sPandyaNadu</styleUrl><description>Thiruthangal, near Sivakasi. Perumal: Nindra Narayanan. Thayar: Senkamala Thayar (Annanayaki). Posture: Standing. A hill temple where Sri Devi stayed (thangal) in penance. Linked with the wedding of Aniruddha and Usha.</description><ExtendedData><Data name="Number"><value>89</value></Data><Data name="Region"><value>Pandya Nadu</value></Data><Data name="Tamil"><value>திருத்தங்கல்</value></Data></ExtendedData><Point><coordinates>77.8853,9.0107,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>90. Thirukkoodal</name><styleUrl>#sPandyaNadu</styleUrl><description>Madurai (Koodal Azhagar). Perumal: Koodal Azhagar. Thayar: Madhuravalli. Posture: Sitting. A three-storey Ashtanga vimanam with the Lord sitting, standing and reclining. Periyazhwar sang Thiruppallandu in this city.</description><ExtendedData><Data name="Number"><value>90</value></Data><Data name="Region"><value>Pandya Nadu</value></Data><Data name="Tamil"><value>திருக்கூடல்</value></Data></ExtendedData><Point><coordinates>78.2643,9.9886,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>91. Thirumaliruncholai</name><styleUrl>#sPandyaNadu</styleUrl><description>Azhagar Koil, near Madurai. Perumal: Paramaswami; utsavar Sundararajan (Kallazhagar). Thayar: Sundaravalli. Posture: Standing. Kallazhagar rides to the Vaigai each Chithirai. Andal vowed a hundred pots of sweet rice here, and Ramanuja fulfilled it for her centuries later.</description><ExtendedData><Data name="Number"><value>91</value></Data><Data name="Region"><value>Pandya Nadu</value></Data><Data name="Tamil"><value>திருமாலிருஞ்சோலை</value></Data></ExtendedData><Point><coordinates>78.2643,9.9886,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>92. Thirumohur</name><styleUrl>#sPandyaNadu</styleUrl><description>Thirumohur, near Madurai. Perumal: Kalameghan. Thayar: Mohanavalli. Posture: Standing. The Lord took the Mohini form here. Nammazhwar calls Him the guide who walks with the soul on its last journey. The Sudarsana shrine is renowned.</description><ExtendedData><Data name="Number"><value>92</value></Data><Data name="Region"><value>Pandya Nadu</value></Data><Data name="Tamil"><value>திருமோகூர்</value></Data></ExtendedData><Point><coordinates>78.2643,9.9886,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>93. Thirukkoshtiyur</name><styleUrl>#sPandyaNadu</styleUrl><description>Thirukoshtiyur (Sowmya Narayana). Perumal: Uraga Mellanayan; utsavar Sowmya Narayanan. Thayar: Thirumamagal Nachiyar. Posture: Reclining. Ramanuja walked here eighteen times to receive the eight-syllable mantra from Thirukoshtiyur Nambi, then shared its meaning openly with all who wished to hear.</description><ExtendedData><Data name="Number"><value>93</value></Data><Data name="Region"><value>Pandya Nadu</value></Data><Data name="Tamil"><value>திருக்கோட்டியூர்</value></Data></ExtendedData><Point><coordinates>78.2643,9.9886,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>94. Thiruppullani</name><styleUrl>#sPandyaNadu</styleUrl><description>Thiruppullani, near Ramanathapuram. Perumal: Adi Jagannathan (Kalyana Jagannathan); Darbha Sayana Raman. Thayar: Kalyanavalli, Padmasani. Posture: Standing, Reclining. Sri Rama lay on a bed of darbha grass here for three days, seeking passage from the ocean. Vibhishana&apos;s surrender is also placed here.</description><ExtendedData><Data name="Number"><value>94</value></Data><Data name="Region"><value>Pandya Nadu</value></Data><Data name="Tamil"><value>திருப்புல்லாணி</value></Data></ExtendedData><Point><coordinates>78.2643,9.9886,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>95. Thirumeyyam</name><styleUrl>#sPandyaNadu</styleUrl><description>Thirumayam (Sathyamurthi). Perumal: Sathyagirinathan (Sathyamurthi); Thirumeyyar. Thayar: Uyyavantha Nachiyar. Posture: Standing, Reclining. A rock-cut cave temple with one of the largest reclining forms, carved from the hill itself.</description><ExtendedData><Data name="Number"><value>95</value></Data><Data name="Region"><value>Pandya Nadu</value></Data><Data name="Tamil"><value>திருமெய்யம்</value></Data></ExtendedData><Point><coordinates>78.2643,9.9886,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark></Folder>
<Folder><name>Vada Nadu</name><Placemark><name>96. Thiruvayodhi</name><styleUrl>#sVadaNadu</styleUrl><description>Ayodhya. Perumal: Sri Raman (Chakravarti Thirumagan). Thayar: Sita. Posture: Standing. Birthplace of Sri Rama on the Sarayu. The Azhwars sing the town itself, without naming a single shrine.</description><ExtendedData><Data name="Number"><value>96</value></Data><Data name="Region"><value>Vada Nadu</value></Data><Data name="Tamil"><value>திருவயோத்தி</value></Data></ExtendedData><Point><coordinates>82.1996,26.8051,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>97. Naimisaranyam</name><styleUrl>#sVadaNadu</styleUrl><description>Neemsar (Naimisharanya). Perumal: Devarajan (Sri Hari). Thayar: Sri Hari Lakshmi (Pundarikavalli). Posture: Standing. The forest itself is worshipped as the Lord. Here Suta Gosvami spoke the Srimad-Bhagavatam to the sages headed by Saunaka.</description><ExtendedData><Data name="Number"><value>97</value></Data><Data name="Region"><value>Vada Nadu</value></Data><Data name="Tamil"><value>நைமிசாரண்யம்</value></Data></ExtendedData><Point><coordinates>80.5705,27.4363,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>98. Thiruppirithi</name><styleUrl>#sVadaNadu</styleUrl><description>Joshimath (traditional identification). Perumal: Paramapurushan. Thayar: Parimalavalli. Posture: Reclining. The first place Thirumangai Azhwar sings in the Periya Thirumozhi. Scholars differ on its exact site, and most pilgrims worship at Joshimath.</description><ExtendedData><Data name="Number"><value>98</value></Data><Data name="Region"><value>Vada Nadu</value></Data><Data name="Tamil"><value>திருப்பிரிதி</value></Data></ExtendedData><Point><coordinates>79.4224,29.9298,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>99. Thirukkandam Kadinagar</name><styleUrl>#sVadaNadu</styleUrl><description>Devaprayag (Raghunathji). Perumal: Neelamegha Perumal (Purushottaman, Raghunathji). Thayar: Pundarikavalli. Posture: Standing. At the meeting of the Alaknanda and Bhagirathi, where the river is first called Ganga. Periyazhwar&apos;s decad praises the Ganga itself.</description><ExtendedData><Data name="Number"><value>99</value></Data><Data name="Region"><value>Vada Nadu</value></Data><Data name="Tamil"><value>திருக்கண்டங்கடிநகர்</value></Data></ExtendedData><Point><coordinates>78.5644,30.1456,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>100. Thiruvadari</name><styleUrl>#sVadaNadu</styleUrl><description>Badrinath (Badarikashrama). Perumal: Badri Narayanan. Thayar: Aravindavalli. Posture: Sitting. Narayana sits in meditation as the teacher of the eight-syllable mantra. Open about May to November. Thirumangai Azhwar urges: go while your body still has strength.</description><ExtendedData><Data name="Number"><value>100</value></Data><Data name="Region"><value>Vada Nadu</value></Data><Data name="Tamil"><value>திருவதரி</value></Data></ExtendedData><Point><coordinates>79.4912,30.7447,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>101. Thiruchalagramam</name><styleUrl>#sVadaNadu</styleUrl><description>Muktinath, on the Gandaki. Perumal: Sri Murti. Thayar: Sri Devi. Posture: Standing. The only Divya Desam outside India, at about 3,700 metres. The Gandaki river is the source of salagrama silas.</description><ExtendedData><Data name="Number"><value>101</value></Data><Data name="Region"><value>Vada Nadu</value></Data><Data name="Tamil"><value>திருச்சாளக்கிராமம்</value></Data></ExtendedData><Point><coordinates>83.8713,28.8167,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>102. Vada Mathura</name><styleUrl>#sVadaNadu</styleUrl><description>Mathura (Sri Krishna Janmasthan). Perumal: Govardhanesan (Balakrishnan). Thayar: Satyabhama. Posture: Standing. Birthplace of Sri Krishna. Andal&apos;s verses long for Mathura, Vrindavana and Govardhana.</description><ExtendedData><Data name="Number"><value>102</value></Data><Data name="Region"><value>Vada Nadu</value></Data><Data name="Tamil"><value>வடமதுரை</value></Data></ExtendedData><Point><coordinates>77.6696,27.5048,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>103. Thiruvaippadi</name><styleUrl>#sVadaNadu</styleUrl><description>Gokula. Perumal: Navamohana Krishnan. Thayar: Rukmini, Satyabhama. Posture: Standing. The cowherd village of Krishna&apos;s childhood. Periyazhwar sings as Yasoda, and Andal becomes a gopi of this village in the Thiruppavai.</description><ExtendedData><Data name="Number"><value>103</value></Data><Data name="Region"><value>Vada Nadu</value></Data><Data name="Tamil"><value>திருவாய்ப்பாடி</value></Data></ExtendedData><Point><coordinates>80.4387,26.9501,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>104. Thiruthuvarai</name><styleUrl>#sVadaNadu</styleUrl><description>Dwaraka (Dwarakadhish). Perumal: Dwarakadhisan (Kalyana Narayanan). Thayar: Kalyana Nachiyar (Rukmini). Posture: Standing. Krishna as king of Dvaraka. Andal asks to be taken to the city of the Lord of sixteen thousand queens.</description><ExtendedData><Data name="Number"><value>104</value></Data><Data name="Region"><value>Vada Nadu</value></Data><Data name="Tamil"><value>திருத்துவாரகை</value></Data></ExtendedData><Point><coordinates>73.3305,24.0099,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>105. Singavel Kundram</name><styleUrl>#sVadaNadu</styleUrl><description>Ahobilam (Nava Narasimha). Perumal: Ahobila Narasimhan (Prahlada Varadan). Thayar: Lakshmi (Amritavalli). Posture: Sitting. Nine forms of Narasimha across a forested hill range, where He appeared from the pillar for Prahlada. Sri Caitanya Mahaprabhu offered prayers here.</description><ExtendedData><Data name="Number"><value>105</value></Data><Data name="Region"><value>Vada Nadu</value></Data><Data name="Tamil"><value>சிங்கவேள்குன்றம்</value></Data></ExtendedData><Point><coordinates>79.1533,15.341,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>106. Thiruvenkadam</name><styleUrl>#sVadaNadu</styleUrl><description>Tirumala and Tirupati. Perumal: Srinivasan (Venkatesa, Thiruvenkatamudaiyan). Thayar: Alarmel Mangai (Padmavati) at Tiruchanur. Posture: Standing. Ten Azhwars sang the Lord of the seven hills. Nammazhwar&apos;s surrender, &quot;Agalakillen&quot;, is offered at these feet.</description><ExtendedData><Data name="Number"><value>106</value></Data><Data name="Region"><value>Vada Nadu</value></Data><Data name="Tamil"><value>திருவேங்கடம்</value></Data></ExtendedData><Point><coordinates>79.4087,13.8339,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark></Folder>
</Document></kml>